I think I've finally figured things out:.  mfs and a mismatched
kernel/userland strikes again

I've been booting my test kernels on a 4.3 box.  With an mfs mount in
/etc/fstab and a 4.3 mount_mfs sitting in /sbin.  As soon as the mfs
mount occurs, things go to hell in a handbasket and lots of memory
gets trashed.  I don't know why it doesn't happen for SMP kernels and
pre SMP integration kernels -- we just "lucky" and some other memory
is trashed there, I guess.

At any rate, -current seems to work on alpha.    


