> Yep. In the meantime the installation of 4.3R from CD completed without a
> hitch.
> 
> It is just that after a reboot I don't seem to have a console.

For a variety of unpleasant reasons, you have to make sure that either
this

zs0     "/usr/libexec/getty std.9600"         vt100  on secure

or

console "/usr/libexec/getty Pc"         cons25  on  secure

is on. 4.3 ships with console 'off'. There's all this bushwa about X and yatta
yatta yatta. The answer was ttyd0 should work. Not. Oh well.

If you do zs, you have to manually make zs, as in

mknod /dev/zs0 c 135 0 root:wheel

as zs isn't in MAKEDEV.



